      'A Task Vector is the difference between model parameters before and after one round of updating. It tells us how much the parameters changed and, when direction is retained, where they moved. We first track the Frobenius magnitude across all 160 rounds, then test whether larger updates are actually associated with higher Task Score after removing the shared trend with training round.',
